 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "U-PZ-MgVAgAJ",
   "from": "Joe Nese",
   "author": "0a059d7bc86e3416",
   "date": "2018-04-03T18:20:19Z",
   "subject": "Sample Covariance Matrix",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I wish to run analyses with the sample covariance matrix. Is there an easier way to enter the data in the matrix than is shown in the example? I have 21 variables, and would just like to use the data from my data, as opposed to entering it by hand (or copy/paste). When I tried to use the data as a vector, I could not get it to work.<br><br>Any help on this minor issue is much appreciated.<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "8EGk3aidAgAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2018-04-05T11:50:14Z",
   "subject": "Re: Sample Covariance Matrix",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">would just like to use the data from my data, as opposed to entering it by hand (or copy/paste)<br></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>You mean raw data, with observations in rows and variables in columns?  Just use the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> data= </font>argument instead.</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/cfa.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/cfa.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425783919000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2d2mQJhNzWONr1u8nePFg_\">http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/cfa.html</a><br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">UvA web page: <a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425783919000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2H6XiAqlOpcQgM-IraJ0JB\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "6a4XhESsAgAJ",
   "from": "Joe Nese",
   "author": "0a059d7bc86e3416",
   "date": "2018-04-05T16:17:56Z",
   "subject": "Re: Sample Covariance Matrix",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I am speaking of the getCov function. I have the covariance matrix of the data (not a typical data table). The tutorial suggests typing in the values by hand, but with 21 variables, it is quite a large matrix (231 values).<br><br>Any thoughts?</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Thursday, April 5, 2018 at 4:50:14 AM UTC-7, Terrence Jorgensen wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">would just like to use the data from my data, as opposed to entering it by hand (or copy/paste)<br></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>You mean raw data, with observations in rows and variables in columns?  Just use the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> data= </font>argument instead.</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/cfa.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/cfa.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425783920000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3eMfDNQT9AXm-77QfS7yoI\">http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/cfa.html</a><br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">UvA web page: <a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425783920000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0zBcuEIjQk4s5CtoFD1no0\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "uSnIDiWABgAJ",
   "from": "kma...@aol.com",
   "author": "ad188126f9138663",
   "date": "2018-04-06T15:01:38Z",
   "subject": "Re: Sample Covariance Matrix",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Joe,<br>It is hard to answer your question because you are telling us where you want to end up but not where you are starting from.<br><br>If you have your raw data in machine readable form or in your workspace already, you can use cov(myData) to obtain the covariance matrix.<br><br>If you do not have your raw data but have a covariance matrix in machine readable form, you can read it in as a text file.<br><br>If you do not have either in a machine readable form, then your need to type the data by hand, it is just a matter of where you prefer to type it.<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#008\">require</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lavaan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Some data to work with</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>bollenData </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">PoliticalDemocracy</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>head</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenData</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Compute a covariance matrix from data</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>bollenCov </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cov</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenData</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>round</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenCov</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># read and write raw data</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>write</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">csv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenData</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Bollen Data.csv&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>bollenDataCopy </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> read</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">csv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Bollen Data.csv&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>head</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenDataCopy</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># read and write covariance matrix</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>write</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">csv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenCov</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Bollen Covariance Matrix.csv&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>bollenCovCopy </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> read</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">csv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Bollen Covariance Matrix.csv&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>bollenCovCopyMatrix </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenCovCopy</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">12</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># eliminate row names read as first variable</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>rownames</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenCovCopyMatrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> colnames</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenCovCopyMatrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># restore row names as row names</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>round</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenCovCopyMatrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Not identical but very close</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>round</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenCov </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> bollenCovCopyMatrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">13</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Further details on data import and export can be found here:<br><br><a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/doc/manuals/R-data.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/doc/manuals/R-data.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425783924000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0k5kS5XV_A8LNyyDQdRWYj\">https://cran.r-project.org/doc/manuals/R-data.html</a><br><br>Keith<br>------------------------<br>Keith A. Markus<br>John Jay College of Criminal Justice, CUNY<br><a href=\"http://jjcweb.jjay.cuny.edu/kmarkus\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://jjcweb.jjay.cuny.edu/kmarkus&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425783924000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0PlmyjCFzo52iFCi39H6d6\">http://jjcweb.jjay.cuny.edu/kmarkus</a><br>Frontiers of Test Validity Theory: Measurement, Causation and Meaning.<br><a href=\"http://www.routledge.com/books/details/9781841692203/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.routledge.com/books/details/9781841692203/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425783924000&amp;usg=AOvVaw31xneZ8Dqq9Rd86WKmSJNj\">http://www.routledge.com/books/details/9781841692203/</a><br><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "mW5GiSGPBgAJ",
   "from": "Joe Nese",
   "author": "0a059d7bc86e3416",
   "date": "2018-04-06T19:36:15Z",
   "subject": "Re: Sample Covariance Matrix",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Keith, you are right, I apologize for not giving a reproducible example. I will not make that mistake the next time.<br><br>Your examples were very helpful, and led me to the answer. I do not have raw data but have a covariance matrix in machine readable form. My issue was that the upper triangle was empty. Thus, I needed to copy/transpose my lower triangle to my upper triangle (and save the row names as the column names). m[upper.tri(m)] &lt;- t(m)[upper.tri(m)]<br><br>This did the trick, and I did not need to apply the getCov() function.<br><br>Thank you again for your answers, I would have moved on otherwise!<br><br>Best.</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Friday, April 6, 2018 at 8:01:38 AM UTC-7, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">kma...@aol.com</a> wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Joe,<br>It is hard to answer your question because you are telling us where you want to end up but not where you are starting from.<br><br>If you have your raw data in machine readable form or in your workspace already, you can use cov(myData) to obtain the covariance matrix.<br><br>If you do not have your raw data but have a covariance matrix in machine readable form, you can read it in as a text file.<br><br>If you do not have either in a machine readable form, then your need to type the data by hand, it is just a matter of where you prefer to type it.<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#008\">require</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lavaan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Some data to work with</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>bollenData </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">PoliticalDemocracy</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>head</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenData</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Compute a covariance matrix from data</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>bollenCov </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cov</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenData</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>round</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenCov</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># read and write raw data</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>write</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">csv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenData</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Bollen Data.csv&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>bollenDataCopy </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> read</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">csv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Bollen Data.csv&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>head</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenDataCopy</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># read and write covariance matrix</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>write</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">csv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenCov</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Bollen Covariance Matrix.csv&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>bollenCovCopy </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> read</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">csv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Bollen Covariance Matrix.csv&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>bollenCovCopyMatrix </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenCovCopy</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">12</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># eliminate row names read as first variable</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>rownames</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenCovCopyMatrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> colnames</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenCovCopyMatrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># restore row names as row names</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>round</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenCovCopyMatrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Not identical but very close</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>round</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bollenCov </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> bollenCovCopyMatrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">13</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Further details on data import and export can be found here:<br><br><a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/doc/manuals/R-data.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/doc/manuals/R-data.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425783929000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1JSbA1fkimsfVli6SygTU6\">https://cran.r-project.org/doc/manuals/R-data.html</a><br><br>Keith<br>------------------------<br>Keith A. Markus<br>John Jay College of Criminal Justice, CUNY<br><a href=\"http://jjcweb.jjay.cuny.edu/kmarkus\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://jjcweb.jjay.cuny.edu/kmarkus&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425783929000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0-2ISxFdsbLk7x7e5kbvUp\">http://jjcweb.jjay.cuny.edu/kmarkus</a><br>Frontiers of Test Validity Theory: Measurement, Causation and Meaning.<br><a href=\"http://www.routledge.com/books/details/9781841692203/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.routledge.com/books/details/9781841692203/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425783929000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Pv1HuFIP0d1w7P7BMyYIA\">http://www.routledge.com/books/details/9781841692203/</a><br><br></div></blockquote></div>"
